{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790346890,"nonce":"rQjkaKE8RotHSLEqY7Iw3n4crH4=","title":"ZynML: a try statement is parsed and then dropped, so its body never runs","message":"ml.zyn builds TypedStatement::Try from `try { } catch E as e { }` (crates/zynml/ml.zyn, try_stmt), and the e2e tests only check that it parses. Nothing lowers Try or Throw: typed_cfg.rs passes it through as a plain statement and SSA's process_statement discards it in its catch-all arm. The try body never executes and no diagnostic is reported. The `catch _` form the grammar comment documents does not parse either.\n\nZynML has no throw, so until an error model exists the statement should lower its body and refuse catch clauses with a diagnostic (or refuse the whole statement).","files":null}]}